# Create Execution Plan — {{REPO_NAME}}

Task: $ARGUMENTS

Read AGENTS.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/quality.md, and relevant ADRs
in docs/decisions/. Check docs/exec-plans/active/ before creating another plan.

Create docs/exec-plans/active/<unique-slug>.md from docs/exec-plans/template.md with:
- OKF frontmatter: `type: Exec Plan`, `title`, one-line `description`,
  `status: draft`, `affects` (module list), `tags` (chosen for this plan,
  reusing tags already in docs/), and
  `generated: {by: pi/plan-prompt, at: <UTC ISO timestamp>}`
- Every template section filled: Summary, Context, Scope, Approach,
  Decisions, Open questions, Changes, Steps, Risks, Verification, Decision log
- Decisions made now: each row names the option turned down
- Open questions answered, or each marked `assumed: …`
- Steps as short `- [ ]` checkboxes, each with indented `files:` and
  `done when:` sub-bullets

A plan is required before editing more than two source files. Docs are exempt.
Summarise the approach and wait for explicit user approval before implementing.
Work from the plan and check off steps as they finish. Pi archives plans with
at least one checked step and no unchecked steps when the run completes.
Do not mark steps complete merely to bypass the gate.
